{
  "slug": "clawcode",
  "name": "Clawcode",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "ClawCode is an open-source plugin that turns otherwise stateless sessions into persistent agents. It adds identity, personality, long-term memory, lifecycle hooks, memory consolidation (“dreaming”), voice support, web hooks, messaging integrations, and a one-way import path from OpenClaw. The goal is to make Claude Code feel less like a fresh assistant on every launch and more like a continuous agent that remembers context, adapts to the user, and maintains a stable sense of self across sessions.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **20 skills**, **6 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (20): `about` (Show the plugin source — name, version, and repo URL), `channels` (Show messaging channel status (WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, iMessage, Slack, Fakechat) and the launch command to load them), `compact` (Flush important session context to daily log (manual memory flush)), `create` (Create a new agent in the current directory with personality files and bootstrap ritual), `crons` (Manage scheduled reminders (crons) — list, add, delete, pause, resume, reconcile, or import from OpenClaw), `doctor` (Run diagnostic checks on the agent workspace), `heartbeat` (Run agent heartbeat — periodic checks, memory consolidation, proactive work), `help` (List available commands the user can invoke), and 12 more\n- **Hooks** (6): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `PreCompact`, `Stop`, `SessionEnd`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `clawcode`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install clawcode@claude-community` from `crisandrews/ClawCode`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 20,
    "hook": 6,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Juan Cristobal Andrews",
